# Witness: a tenth mark published in a row that omits the leading pipe

The legend is the document every other review document links to instead of repeating, so a
mark added to it reopens the vocabulary the whole rule exists to close. All nine are published
below, and a tenth is added in a row written without the optional leading pipe - one character
short of the shape a scan gated on that pipe can see.

## 1. How To Use This File

### Evidence verdicts - set by the author, about evidence

| Mark | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `[MET]` | Demonstrated. |
| `[PART]` | Partly demonstrated. |
| `[UNMET]` | Not discharged. |
| `[N/A]` | Not claimed at this milestone. |

### Review verdicts - set by the reviewer, about their own reading

| Mark | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `[ ]` | Not yet reviewed. |
| `[A]` | Accepted as stated. |
| `[C]` | Accepted with a condition. |
| `[R]` | Rejected. |
| `[?]` | Cannot be judged from what is here. |
`[WAIVED]` | A tenth mark, published without the optional leading pipe. |
